# One commit per file

When the user asks to commit:

1. Stage and commit **exactly one file** per commit.
2. Repeat until every intended file has its own commit.
3. Message focuses on **why** that file changed; name the file when useful.
4. Never bundle unrelated files. A rename/move that git records as delete+add
   of the same path may share one commit; otherwise still one path per commit.
5. Do not commit unless the user explicitly asked.
